---
description: Increment and synchronize the VS Code plugin patch version for every feature or fix
alwaysApply: true
---

# VS Code patch version

- Every completed user-visible VS Code plugin feature or bug fix increments the
  patch component by exactly one (for example, `0.46.49` → `0.46.50`).
- Treat one delivered batch as one increment, regardless of how many files it
  changes. Do not increment for documentation-only, test-only, formatting, or
  refactoring work that changes no behavior.
- Read the current version from `editors/vscode/package.json`; never infer it
  from a roadmap phase number or git tag.
- Keep these version declarations synchronized:
  - `editors/vscode/package.json`
  - the root package entries in `editors/vscode/package-lock.json`
  - `source/internal/editorhost/proto.go`
  - shipped-version references in project and VS Code README/roadmap docs
- Perform the bump before packaging, smoke-testing, or installing the VSIX so
  the artifact filename and embedded Host version use the new patch number.
